1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,620
My morning routine right now is simple and easy going so I can start the day off right.
我现在的晨间流程简单、轻松，让一天有个好的开始。

2
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:12,420
I wash my face I brush my teeth then I do a quick skincare routine which is just currently cleanser toner than day lotion.
我洗脸、刷牙，然后快速护肤，目前就是洁面、爽肤水和日间乳液。

3
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:19,500
Taking just a few minutes for your skin every morning is just so important to keep your skin as healthy as it can be as we age.
他说，每天早晨花几分钟护肤，对随着年龄增长保持皮肤健康很重要。

4
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,640
Then I fix up my bed hair blow dry it and throw on some wax.
接着我整理睡乱的头发，吹干，再抹点发蜡。

5
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:27,110
This is my partner's pink blow dryer just in case you're wondering.
这是我伴侣的粉色吹风机，免得你们好奇。

6
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:37,079
Then onto a quick breakfast I'm still brewing tea instead of coffee and today I'm making a mug of hojija tea which is a roasted green tea.
然后快速吃早饭；我仍然喝茶而不是咖啡，今天泡一杯烘焙绿茶。

7
00:00:37,079 --> 00:00:40,669
Then I'm making a quick bowl of oats with nuts and raisins.
然后做一碗燕麦，加些坚果和葡萄干。

8
00:00:40,679 --> 00:00:45,300
Sometimes I'll cook a proper breakfast and other times I'll go out for breakfast.
有时候我会认真做一顿早餐，其他时候就出去吃。

9
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:48,709
It really depends on what I have on for the day.
这主要取决于当天有什么安排。

10
00:00:48,719 --> 00:00:54,780
I often try and take this time to have breakfast with my partner who also has flexibility in her schedule.
我经常尽量利用这段时间和伴侣一起吃早餐，她的日程也比较灵活。

11
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:58,560
Working for a tech startup and is also working for herself on the side.
她在一家科技初创公司工作，同时也做自己的事业。

12
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:01,320
She's a talented cookie and I'm really proud of her.
她很有才干，我真为她骄傲。

13
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:07,260
And we take this chance to just chat about all sorts of random things like what was the first ever state of the us.
我们趁机随便聊各种事，比如美国最早的州是哪一个。

14
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:09,180
Let me know down below if you know.
如果知道，就在下面告诉我。

15
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:15,110
Right after I'll spend about 20 to 30 minutes checking and replying to urgent emails.
紧接着，我会花大约二三十分钟查看并回复紧急邮件。

16
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,519
Since my clients are literally all across the globe.
因为我的客户真的是遍布全球。

17
00:01:17,519 --> 00:01:26,509
I'm working with time zones like california new York and israel to singapore and hong kong but more about that when I actually get into the office.
我要配合从加州、纽约、以色列到新加坡、香港的时区；到办公室后再详细聊。

18
00:01:26,519 --> 00:01:31,670
And then I'll fit in a push or pull session at the gym for about 45 minutes.
然后我会挤出大约45分钟，到健身房做一次推或拉的训练。

19
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:35,519
I just feel a lot more fresh and happier fitting in exercise.
安排上运动后，我觉得更精神，也更开心。

20
00:01:35,519 --> 00:01:39,239
But I don't always get the chance to depending on how busy my schedule is.
但我并非总有机会，要看日程有多忙。

21
00:01:39,239 --> 00:01:42,720
One of the things I love about being my own boss is setting my own hours.
自己当老板，我喜欢的一点是可以决定自己的工作时间。

22
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,659
Even though I often work 12 to 14 hour days.
尽管我常常一天工作12到14个小时。

23
00:01:45,659 --> 00:01:50,820
Had a good session at the gym I'm now gonna go to the new office which I'll show you guys in a moment.
刚才练得不错，我现在要去新办公室，马上带你们看看。

24
00:01:50,820 --> 00:01:54,960
But yeah going to the gym is really important big part of the morning routine.
不过，去健身房确实是我晨间流程里很重要的一部分。

25
00:01:54,960 --> 00:02:02,000
I usually supplement the gym because it gets kind of boring sometimes with f 45 kickboxing bouldering that sort of stuff.
因为有时健身房会有点无聊，我通常还会补充F45、自由搏击、抱石这类活动。

26
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:09,110
So that's now all wrapped up I'm now gonna finally get into work so let's head over to the office.
现在这些都结束了，我终于要开始工作了，去办公室吧。

27
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:12,780
So welcome to the new office and studio I've just moved into.
欢迎来到我刚搬进来的新办公室和工作室。

28
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:15,180
At this point it's usually 9 to 10 a m.
到这个时候，通常是上午九到十点。

29
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:17,760
This is a property I purchased a few years ago.
这处房产是我几年前买下的。

30
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:24,540
But more recently I've been working on transforming this space so I'm able to make use of it while the media company continues to grow.
不过最近我一直在改造这里，方便在传媒公司持续成长时利用这个空间。

31
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:26,159
It's still a work in progress.
它还在逐步完善中。

32
00:02:26,159 --> 00:02:32,099
So if you want to follow on in this setup makeover series I'll leave a link to the videos below if you want to check it out.
想追这个布置改造系列的话，我会在下面放视频链接，欢迎去看看。

33
00:02:32,099 --> 00:02:34,140
Anyway I'm just setting up on my desk.
总之，我现在在桌前准备开工。

34
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:41,210
It's not a work day without good music though so first things first lo fi music.
工作日可不能没有好音乐，所以先来点低保真音乐。

35
00:02:43,159 --> 00:02:47,929
This is my current office corner and desk setup where I do most of my work.
这就是我现在的办公角和桌面布置，大部分工作都在这里完成。

36
00:02:47,939 --> 00:02:55,379
From really mundane stuff like emails and admin work to the more creative things like filming photography and marketing and design work.
从邮件、行政这些日常琐事，到拍摄、摄影、营销、设计这类创作工作。

37
00:02:55,379 --> 00:03:01,500
In case you're a new subscriber here or you're just curious about what I do because that seems to be a pretty common question.
如果你刚订阅，或只是好奇我做什么——这似乎是常被问到的问题。

38
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:06,419
I currently run a four person media company everyone's working remotely.
我目前经营一家四人传媒公司，大家都远程办公。

39
00:03:06,419 --> 00:03:10,380
But I'm trying to do a better team actually of bring people in house.
但我在努力把团队做得更好，实际把人招到内部一起工作。

40
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:17,390
So I think I'm going to start beginning to hire people full time to work with me alongside me.
所以我想开始招聘全职员工，让他们和我一起工作。
